  {
   "id": 15188653343099,
   "title": "Jack's Mac - Black",
   "handle": "the-jacks-mac-black",
   "body_html": "<div class=\"product-description\">\n<div class=\"left-column\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">100% waterproof</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">Unlined</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">Regular fit</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">Inset sleeves</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">8-gauge centre front copper zip with additional stud fastening<br>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">Copper taped internal seams</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">Military grade copper hardware from RIRI of Switzerland</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">Two internal stud secure pockets</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">Vandyke stitched collar</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">Etched copper rivets on back neck and hanger loop</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">Ventile® stud bearer with hold tab at the base to ease zip fastening</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">As a natural, piece-dyed cotton, Ventile® will likely develop a soft patina and gentle colour fading over time, a hallmark of its character and heritage</li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\">Made in our own factory in Manchester, England<br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Model's measurements: Height: 6’1/185cm, Chest: 40\"/101cm, Waist: 34\"/86cm and wears a Size 4/M</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<!-- split -->\n<h4><strong>FABRIC</strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\"><span> 100% cotton - and for many the best cotton in the world</span></li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\"><span>200 grams per square metre</span></li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\"><span> 81 threads per cm (warp) and 30 threads per cm (weft)</span></li>\n<li style=\"list-style: disc;\"><span> Ventile® was developed near our Manchester factory at the direct request from Winston Churchill during World War II</span></li>\n</ul>\n<strong>CARE INSTRUCTIONS</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Specialist dry clean only (be mindful of the sealing tape)</li>\n<li>Wipe down as required</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
   "published_at": "2025-09-03T11:55:41+01:00",
